# Comment Standards

Density / pseudocode examples (Read when commenting or auditing):
`skills/twincat3-code-style/references/comment-rules.md`

## Principles

1. **Only `(* *)`** — never `//` in ST CDATA. English only. Nested pairs allowed.
2. **FB / FUNCTION / PROGRAM header** — `(* … *)` above declaration (purpose/contracts). One line OK for simple FBs; no decorative banners unless the file already uses them.
3. **VAR_INPUT / VAR_OUTPUT** — every member has EOL `(* *)`. Units in brackets when useful (`[A]`, `[W]`, `[%]`). BOOL: describe TRUE meaning. Do not repeat the identifier.
4. **VAR** — section headers for large/grouped blocks; EOL only for non-obvious members. Small blocks (<5) need no header.
5. **Implementation** — short prose before phases (why / order / invariant). Prefer prose over dash banners; dash banners only if file already uses them. Do not narrate obvious code.
6. **CASE** — every case label: inline `(* purpose *)` (no step-number echo).
7. **Methods / Actions** — header when contract/OC/order matters; skip trivial helpers.
8. **STRUCT** — every member EOL `(* *)`; section headers when large; purpose above `TYPE` when non-trivial.
9. **ENUM** — every enumerator EOL `(* *)`; keep attributes unchanged.
10. **Do not** — comment `END_*`, name-only echoes, TODO without owner+date, every private VAR, whole-library silent rewrites.

Per-object workflow: skill `twincat3-comment` / `/twincat3-cmd-comment`.
